  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Essentials**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core project files: `metadata.json`, `package.json`, and the requirements. I want to build out the project essentials and architecture around these files and the initial brief. The focus is to clearly define the fundamental structure of the AI aggregator for Bangladeshi users, keeping in mind the need for easy access via a single chat interface.\n\n\n**Defining Core Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the key features: user accounts with subscriptions and chat history, along with an admin panel. I\'ve decided all user-facing text should be in Bangla, with English as secondary. The currency is set to Bangladeshi Taka, with clearly defined monthly and yearly subscription plans. I\'ve also detailed how subscription access should be managed, along with usage limits.\n\n\n**Outlining Public Interfaces**\n\nI\'m now outlining the public-facing components. I\'m focusing on the \"Home,\" \"About,\" and \"Privacy Policy\" pages. The homepage will include a hero section, feature showcase, pricing comparisons in Bangladeshi Taka (\340\247\263), and testimonials. I\'ve drafted \"About Us\" and \"Privacy Policy\" pages as well. I\'m building out a sensible draft of the privacy policy, noting that it should be reviewed by a legal professional.\n\n\n**Securing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing secure authentication. I am planning on using robust password hashing with salt, and JWT or secure token handling. I\'m also preparing pre-seeded demo accounts for testing: admin, active subscriber, and a free user.\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user account page. This will include profile information, subscription status, renewal details, and a usage progress bar. I\'m including upgrade/renew buttons, along with billing and payment history.\nI\'m also working on the chat interface, and will be providing a minimal layout. There will be a collapsible sidebar and the option to rename chats.\n\n\n**Detailing Chat Features**\n\nI am now outlining the chat interface design in full. I\'ve detailed the deletion of chats, search, and pinned/recent chat features. I am envisioning a centered input area with a textarea that resizes automatically and includes prompt suggestions in Bangla. I\'ve also detailed simulated file/image attachments, a stop generation button, a clear model selector with badges (\340\246\246\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\244, \340\246\257\340\247\201\340\246\225\340\247\215\340\246\244\340\246\277, \340\246\225\340\247\213\340\246\241\340\246\277\340\246\202), and real-time streaming text with markdown. I\'m also now planning for usage deduction and theme toggles. I have also detailed Bangladeshi payment gateways.\n\n\n**Implementing Payment Processing**\n\nNow, I\'m working on the payment processing. I\'m focusing on TrxID verification, instant payment gateway mockups, plan activation, and expiry date calculation, including 30-day and 365-day plans and renewals. I\'m also preparing the admin panel, with RBAC to manage users, subscriptions, AI providers, usage limits, and revenue dashboards.\n\n\n"
