    thinking: "**Updating Project Metadata**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `metadata.json` and `index.html` files. The app will be called \"Bangla AI\" (\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276 \340\246\217\340\246\206\340\246\207 - \340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\340\246\246\340\247\207\340\246\266\340\247\207\340\246\260 \340\246\270\340\247\207\340\246\260\340\246\276 \340\246\217\340\246\206\340\246\207 \340\246\256\340\246\241\340\247\207\340\246\262 \340\246\271\340\246\276\340\246\254). Its description highlights it as a single platform for top AI models tailored to Bangladeshi users, offering superfast chat in both Bangla and English. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate and compelling metadata.\n\n\n**Defining User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now outlining key user journeys for Bangla AI, focusing on both non-subscriber and subscriber experiences. I\'ve broken down each journey into specific steps, identifying what a user should visibly see after each action. Specifically, I\'m verifying the subscription flow including simulated payments, and confirming subscriber access to different AI models and language support. This includes Bangla input and output.\n\n\n**Mapping User Flow**\n\nI\'m currently mapping the user flow for a specific interaction - a user requesting a response, which will be streamed in markdown. Usage token deduction and visibility are in the works, and conversations should save in the sidebar, which creates a new chat as well. I\'m also focused on the admin panel, including logging in as admin and making configurations. I have the new screen names: Homepage, About Us, Privacy Policy, Authentication, Account Dashboard, and the Chat App.\n\n\n"
