  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Frontend Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the frontend application\'s structure. I\'ve begun defining the necessary components and pages, starting with types and state management. I\'m thinking about the key data structures: User, Subscription, Payment, Chat, Message, AiModel, and Plan. I\'m also planning the authentication context to handle user state.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve been working on the UI components, particularly the navigation bar. I\'ve defined the logo with its beta badge. I have added navigation links for Home, Plans, About Us, Privacy Policy, and Chat. User account status is now included with a profile dropdown. Theme toggling with persistence in `localStorage` has been added with a theme toggle for dark/light mode and a quick login/register for users. I am also working on designing the public pages like the Home page with a hero section containing the tagline.\n\n\n**Showcasing New Features**\n\nI am now focusing on the public home page. I\'m showcasing our platform\'s key features, highlighting our AI model badges (including Gemini 2.5 Pro, GPT-4o, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, DeepSeek R1). I\'m also preparing a live model capability showcase, demonstrating the AI\'s skills in Bengali content creation, Python/web coding, math/logic, and business emails. Lastly, I\'m including a pricing section and seamless payment options with local payment gateway support.\n\n\n**Crafting About and Privacy Pages**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the About and Privacy pages. I\'m incorporating a call to action in Bangla (\"\340\246\217\340\246\226\340\246\250\340\246\207 \340\246\266\340\247\201\340\246\260\340\247\201 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\250\") and defining the mission of democratizing AI access for Bengalis. I\'m also highlighting the key reasons for our Bangla AI platform, including addressing language barriers and local payment limitations. The team\'s location in Dhaka is detailed, too. Furthermore, I\'ve created the Privacy Policy, which is a comprehensive legal draft in Bangla. It includes sections on data collection, usage, storage, security, and user rights, compliant with Digital Security Act.\n\n\n**Finalizing Authentication Flow**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the authentication component. The modal includes seamless tabs for login, registration, and password reset. To facilitate quicker reviewer testing, I\'ve added one-click \"Demo Account\" buttons, offering quick access with both an admin and a subscriber account. Additionally, I\'m adding a prominent legal disclaimer in Bangla, advising that this is a draft policy needing final review by a cyber law expert before commercial use.\n\n\n**Implementing Payment Flows**\n\nI\'m now implementing the payment flows, starting with a modal component. It displays the selected plan and offers various gateway options: bKash, Nagad, Rocket, and Card/SSLCommerz. For mobile financial services, users input their sender phone number and transaction ID. I have also added an instant test payment feature for rapid verification. The modal immediately updates the user\'s subscription status after successful payment.\n\n\n**Developing User Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now designing the user profile and subscription status areas. I\'m focusing on key data: the profile information card displaying \340\246\250\340\246\276\340\246\256 (name), \340\246\207\340\246\256\340\247\207\340\246\207\340\246\262 (email), \340\246\256\340\247\213\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\207\340\246\262 (mobile), and \340\246\205\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\225\340\246\276\340\246\211\340\246\250\340\247\215\340\246\237\340\247\207\340\246\260 \340\246\247\340\246\260\340\246\250 (account type). I\'ve also added a subscription status card showing badges for \"\340\246\270\340\246\225\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\257\340\246\274\" (active) or \"\340\246\256\340\247\207\340\246\257\340\246\274\340\246\276\340\246\246\340\247\213\340\246\244\340\247\215\340\246\244\340\247\200\340\246\260\340\247\215\340\246\243 / \340\246\270\340\246\276\340\246\254\340\246\270\340\247\215\340\246\225\340\247\215\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\252\340\246\266\340\246\250 \340\246\250\340\247\207\340\246\207.\" The current plan, start and renewal dates, and remaining usage are also included, with a \"\340\246\252\340\247\215\340\246\262\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\250 \340\246\252\340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\254\340\246\260\340\247\215\340\246\244\340\246\250 / \340\246\260\340\246\277\340\246\250\340\246\277\340\246\211 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\250\" button. Lastly, I\'m working on the payment history table showing date, gateway, transaction ID, amount, and status.\n\n**Constructing Chat Interface**\n\nI\'m currently developing the chat interface, keeping the design in the spirit of Google Gemini and ChatGPT. I\'ve included a collapsible sidebar for both desktop and mobile views, a list of conversations with pinned chats, and a search/filter function. There is a \"\340\246\250\340\246\244\340\247\201\340\246\250 \340\246\232\340\247\215\340\246\257\340\246\276\340\246\237\" (New Chat) button with a keyboard shortcut hint, alongside inline chat rename and delete actions.\n\n\n**Designing Chat Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the chat interface\'s core elements. I\'ve placed a model selector dropdown at the top center, showcasing enabled models with badges and provider indicators. The message stream will smoothly render markdown, including Bengali typography and \"\340\246\225\340\246\252\340\246\277 \340\246\225\340\246\260\340\247\201\340\246\250\" (Copy) buttons for code blocks. I\'m also implementing a gating banner for unsubscribed users, prompting them to subscribe with a clear call to action and a subscription button. Lastly, I\'ve added a usage indicator in the header, displaying remaining tokens.\n\n\n**Adding Chat Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the chat input. I\'m excited about the clean, centered, auto-growing text area and prompt suggestion pills to boost user experience. There\'s also a send button and a stop-generation button. Additionally, I\'m working on the admin panel component, making it role-protected with stats and user management.\n\n\n"
