    thinking: "**Examining Auth Implementation**\n\nI\'ve successfully deployed the rules; that part is complete! Now, I\'m digging into the authentication implementation, starting with creating `src/firebase.ts`. It\'ll initialize the Firebase app using `firebase-applet-config.json` and export `auth`, `db`, and `googleProvider`. I\'ll also add those helper functions like `loginWithGoogle()` and `logoutFirebase()`.\n\n\n**Verifying Firebase Connection**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Firebase initialization code, exactly as specified in `firebase-integration-rpc`. I\'m paying close attention to importing the necessary modules, setting up the `db` and `auth` exports, and using the configurations. I\'ve also noted the critical line related to the database ID. I\'m building out a `testConnection` function to validate the Firestore connection upon application startup.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_17733421316814861722"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { initializeApp } from \'firebase/app\';\\nimport { \\n  getAuth, \\n  GoogleAuthProvider, \\n  signInWithPopup, \\n  signOut as firebaseSignOut,\\n  onAuthStateChanged,\\n  User as FirebaseUser\\n} from \'firebase/auth\';\\nimport { getFirestore, doc, getDocFromServer } from \'firebase/firestore\';\\nimport firebaseConfig from \'../firebase-applet-config.json\';\\n\\n// Initialize Firebase App\\nconst app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\\n\\n// Initialize Firestore with custom database ID from config\\nexport const db = getFirestore(app, firebaseConfig.firestoreDatabaseId);\\n\\n// Initialize Firebase Auth\\nexport const auth = getAuth(app);\\n\\n// Google Auth Provider\\nexport const googleProvider = new GoogleAuthProvider();\\ngoogleProvider.setCustomParameters({\\n  prompt: \'select_account\'\\n});\\n\\n// Validate Connection to Firestore on startup\\nasync function testConnection() {\\n  try {\\n    await getDocFromServer(doc(db, \'test\', \'connection\'));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes(\'the client is offline\')) {\\n      console.warn(\'Firebase client appears offline or connecting:\', error.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\ntestConnection();\\n\\n// Sign in with Google Popup\\nexport async function signInWithGoogle(): Promise<{ user: FirebaseUser; token: string }> {\\n  const result = await signInWithPopup(auth, googleProvider);\\n  const token = await result.user.getIdToken();\\n  return { user: result.user, token };\\n}\\n\\n// Sign out from Firebase\\nexport async function signOutFromFirebase(): Promise<void> {\\n  await firebaseSignOut(auth);\\n}\\n\\nexport { onAuthStateChanged };\\nexport type { FirebaseUser };\\n\", \"Description\":\"Firebase initialization with Auth and Firestore instances\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/firebase.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating src/firebase.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write firebase.ts\"}"
