  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding User Attributes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating Firebase user attributes into the `DatabaseData` and related interfaces. I\'ve decided to add `firebase_uid?: string;` and `avatar_url?: string;` to the `User` interface within both `src/db/database.ts` and `src/types/index.ts`. Next, I will be adding a `getUserByFirebase` method to the `Database` class.\n\n\n**Refining User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now refining the user authentication flow. I\'ve updated `getUserByEmail` and am considering how to bootstrap the system by making the user `rakib504254@gmail.com` an admin upon login with a high quota. I\'ve verified real users can register and sign in with Google, obtaining the necessary data from the frontend. The server-side logic now includes checks for existing users, assigning admin roles based on email and handling new user creation including a check on the email for setting `role = admin` if the email matches.\n\n\n**Implementing User Features**\n\nI\'m currently working on enhancing user functionality. My focus is now on incorporating initial user state upon account creation. This involves setting role-based defaults: `\'admin\' : \'user\'`, \'active\' status, and usage limits. I\'m dynamically assigning these initial states, including a high usage limit for the admin. I will also incorporate logic for subscriptions. I will also make updates to the AuthModal to integrate the Google sign-in system and remove demo sign-in and dummy forms.\n\n\n**Designing Google Auth Flow**\n\nI\'m now designing the Google Auth flow within a modern modal. It will feature a prominent \"Continue with Google\" button with the Google logo, clearly indicating the use of Google authentication for both sign-in and sign-up. It must handle sign-in, sign-out, clear error feedback, and seamless state updates. I will integrate this into `AuthContext.tsx` by adding `loginWithGoogle`. I\'m using `signInWithGoogle()` and making API calls for authentication.\n\n\n"
